Fernanda, your question made me think about how I might go about<br>trying to preserve the file names on concordance results after<br>converting files from PDF to text. Here&#39;s what I wrote in answer to<br>that question. (Excuse the overload on detail, but that&#39;s how I write<br>my scripts.) Best of luck. Earl Brown<br><br>############################<br># this section converts PDF to text and then loads each text file into<br>R and search them<br><br>rm(list=ls(all=T))<br><br># loads the function exact matches<br>source(file=&quot;/Users/brow2662/Documents/_qclwr/fn_em2.r&quot;)<br><br># gets the file names with a .pdf extension<br>file.names&lt;-dir(&quot;/Users/brow2662/Documents/test_pdf_conversion&quot;,<br>pattern=&quot;.pdf$&quot;, full.names=T)<br><br># creates a collector for all results<br>all.results&lt;-character()<br><br># defines search.term<br>search.term&lt;-&quot;\bfrequency\b&quot;<br><br># loop to convert PDF to text and then search for search.term<br>for (i in file.names) {<br><br>	# progress report<br>	cat(&quot;Working on &quot;, basename(i), &quot;
&quot;, sep=&quot;&quot;)<br><br>	# gets current file name<br>	<a href="http://current.file.name" target="_blank" rel="nofollow" data-saferedirecturl="https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://current.file.name&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792492090065000&amp;usg=AOvVaw10fkA-q019v8hG3l3fr4_X">current.file.name</a>&lt;-basename(i)<br>	<a href="http://current.file.name" target="_blank" rel="nofollow" data-saferedirecturl="https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://current.file.name&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792492090065000&amp;usg=AOvVaw10fkA-q019v8hG3l3fr4_X">current.file.name</a>&lt;-sub(&quot;\.pdf&quot;, &quot;&quot;, <a href="http://current.file.name" target="_blank" rel="nofollow" data-saferedirecturl="https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://current.file.name&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792492090065000&amp;usg=AOvVaw10fkA-q019v8hG3l3fr4_X">current.file.name</a>,<br>ignore.case=T, perl=T)<br><br>	# sets the three arguments for the call to system()<br>	function.location&lt;-&quot;/usr/local/bin/pdftotext&quot;<br>	input.file&lt;-paste(&quot;&#39;&quot;, i, &quot;&#39;&quot;, sep=&quot;&quot;)<br>	output.file&lt;-paste(&quot;/Users/brow2662/Documents/test_pdf_conversion/&quot;,<br><a href="http://current.file.name" target="_blank" rel="nofollow" data-saferedirecturl="https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://current.file.name&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792492090065000&amp;usg=AOvVaw10fkA-q019v8hG3l3fr4_X">current.file.name</a>, &quot;.txt&quot;, sep=&quot;&quot;)<br><br>	# converts current PDF to text<br>	system(paste(function.location, input.file, output.file, sep=&quot; &quot;))<br><br>	# creates the pathway to the newly created text file<br>	<a href="http://current.file.text.name" target="_blank" rel="nofollow" data-saferedirecturl="https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://current.file.text.name&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792492090065000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2Q_Y95IdWRYxUFNcGLAq4A">current.file.text.name</a>&lt;-sub(&quot;.pdf$&quot;, &quot;.txt&quot;, i, ignore.case=T,<br>perl=T)<br><br>	# loads the newly created text file into R and converts it to unicode<br>	current.file&lt;-scan(file=<a href="http://current.file.text.name" target="_blank" rel="nofollow" data-saferedirecturl="https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://current.file.text.name&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792492090065000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2Q_Y95IdWRYxUFNcGLAq4A">current.file.text.name</a>, what=&quot;char&quot;,<br>sep=&quot;
&quot;, quote=&quot;&quot;, comment.char=&quot;&quot;, quiet=T)<br>	current.file&lt;-iconv(current.file, &quot;LATIN1&quot;, &quot;UTF-8&quot;)<br><br>	# searches the current text for search.term and gets the context<br>delimited matches<br>	current.results&lt;-exact.matches(search.term, current.file, pcre=T,<br>case.sens=F, characters.around=50)[[4]]<br><br>	# if no hits in current file, goes to next file<br>	if (length(current.results)==0) {<br>		next<br>	}<br><br>	# adds the current file name before the results<br>	current.results&lt;-paste(<a href="http://current.file.name" target="_blank" rel="nofollow" data-saferedirecturl="https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://current.file.name&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792492090065000&amp;usg=AOvVaw10fkA-q019v8hG3l3fr4_X">current.file.name</a>, current.results, sep=&quot;	&quot;)<br><br>	# adds current results to all results<br>	all.results&lt;-append(all.results, current.results)<br><br>} # next file<br><br># saves all results to hard drive<br>cat(&quot;FILE	PRE	HIT	FOL&quot;, all.results, file=&quot;/Users/brow2662/<br>Documents/test_pdf_conversion/results_search.txt&quot;, sep=&quot;
&quot;)<br><br># announces finish<br>cat(&quot;\aAll done!
&quot;)<br><br>############################<br>
